Implement user story SKY-002-a: Implement SkyscannerClient class with typed interfaces and mock mode

## Story Description
Create src/skyscanner/client.ts exporting SkyscannerClient class, SearchParams and FlightResult interfaces. Constructor accepts optional apiKey (falls back to RAPIDAPI_KEY env var, throws if neither present/valid). searchFlights uses global fetch, rejects on HTTP errors and malformed responses. Supports opt-in mock mode via MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API='true' env var returning deterministic fixture data without network calls.

## Acceptance Criteria
- SkyscannerClient class exported with constructor({ apiKey?: string }); apiKey stored as private field (# or private), not publicly readable
- SearchParams interface exported with exactly: origin: string, destination: string, date: string, adults?: number
- FlightResult interface exported with exactly: price: number, currency: string, airline: string, departure: string, arrival: string, duration: number, stops: number
- searchFlights uses Node.js 18+ global fetch exclusively — no axios, node-fetch, or other HTTP library imported
- Constructor throws descriptive Error when no apiKey provided and RAPIDAPI_KEY is unset or empty string; empty-string apiKey arg treated same as omitted; constructor-provided apiKey takes precedence over RAPIDAPI_KEY env var
- searchFlights rejects on HTTP 4xx/5xx with Error including status code in message; error message never contains apiKey value
- searchFlights rejects with descriptive parse/validation Error when response body is malformed or missing expected fields
- When MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API env var equals exactly 'true', searchFlights returns deterministic non-empty FlightResult[] fixture (≥2 results, valid shape, varying prices) without calling fetch; when env var is unset, empty, or any non-'true' value, behaves identically to normal real-fetch mode; real failures are never silently replaced with mock data





